uuid":"bb6327e3-100f-4d76-a179-0bfa47f7e4c2","position":{"commit_sha":"b60e963ac1c9b88a76da27f43e5166b0d286cd8b","position":"1786825078183391001-bb6327e3-100f-4d76-a179-0bfa47f7e4c2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cfafe0e981e79fbb4551386d1d7bf9c9491f4141f7e539348c085b2c45c0ad09","event_uuid":"9987e752-d641-446f-80a9-e029a50993ca","position":{"commit_sha":"ea6198113379cde5f22ded6ce8a73dfbcb1a133f","position":"1786825315549594001-9987e752-d641-446f-80a9-e029a50993ca"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a5a21f65c799d38548738d3a0ddc38ec27653b0b793e128451553c38c6c887c5","event_uuid":"eb184665-52cf-4c9f-b0d8-c6442c7eed4e","position":{"commit_sha":"15853be5556defa76f2cfb255404be5dc8fd6203","position":"1786825462768680001-eb184665-52cf-4c9f-b0d8-c6442c7eed4e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b72b48e20bc9a0a202a5c19d1bcebc4b41041c530844fc3327ee79c75855683d","event_uuid":"d23a7d8b-5d53-454f-84df-b2fc5ab51789","position":{"commit_sha":"198467eb17b3daf256ce7565bef62c50ba5048eb","position":"1786825693713060577-d23a7d8b-5d53-454f-84df-b2fc5ab51789"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and pushed: Gerrit change 1822 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1822), commit cddc460463, patchset 1. Lock-only diff (uv.lock 9+/9-): json-repair 0.63.0, genai-prices 0.1.2, botocore 1.43.69; mcp stayed 1.29.0; pyproject untouched. NOTE: a plain 'uv lock --upgrade-package' resolved PAST the PR (0.63.2/0.1.3/1.43.72); re-locked with exact '==' pins to the PR's reviewed versions to stay inside the certified plan scope — the newer patches will arrive in the next dependabot round. Gates: make lint + make typecheck green, uv lock --check green, targeted usage-surface tests 109 passed + test_llm_capabilities 27 passed (full tests/unit is CI's job per the plan; host env failures documented on dc89-cd11-acd6-4e61). STOP rule not triggered — all three landed (AC2b vacuously satisfied). Epic 732b urgency comment posted (v2 stable / v1.x maintenance-mode). PR #128 commented with the rejection rationale + change link, left open. Ticket stays in_progress pending LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1786824524982378001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"SCOPE ADDITION executed (operator-approved): .github/dependabot.yml uv block now carries ignore [{dependency-name: mcp, update-types: [version-update:semver-major]}] — semver-major only, so 1.x patch/security bumps still flow and security alerts stay on; header comment block gained the one-line 732b rationale + removal trigger. Plan amended (step 7 + AC7, file_impact now 2 paths); first re-review BLOCKED on a real gap (all-three-fail abandon path contradicted AC7) — reconciled: on total STOP, the ignore rule still lands as a standalone dependabot.yml-only change. Re-review PASS + certified (signed_at 1786825315…). Amended into the same change: Gerrit 1822 patchset 2, commit 0d86a2c82e (2 files: uv.lock 9+/9-, dependabot.yml +6/comment +3). YAML validated; make lint green on the amended tree. LLM-Review +1 re-voted on ps2 at push; awaiting Verified. Ticket stays in_progress.","timestamp":1786825462768680001}],"created_at":1786823914792440001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"454d5ebd-e3c7-46d9-bcea-4fd4fb4e4af8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dc89-cd11-acd6-4e61"},{"link_uuid":"ebaacfc9-63ea-46a3-9c3f-2037003b5cbd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3575-ea88-7b51-43c8"},{"link_uuid":"d23a7d8b-5d53-454f-84df-b2fc5ab51789","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f700-8510-7823-4f27"}],"description":"# Land PR #128 safe subset via Gerrit: json-repair 0.63.0 + genai-prices 0.1.2 + botocore 1.43.69; mcp 2.0 deferred to 732b (4th re-proposal)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nGitHub is a read-only mirror: dependabot PRs never merge there; content is re-applied\nlocally and landed via Gerrit, then the PR is closed. PR #128 (branch\n`dependabot/uv/uv-lock-bfcc8af838`) proposes 4 uv-lock updates:\n\n* `mcp` `1.29.0` -> `2.0.0` (MAJOR) — the FOURTH re-proposal (PRs #124/#125/#127),\n  rejected each time under ticket 1dfd-…: mcp 2.0 renames `FastMCP` -> `MCPServer`,\n  replaces transport+`ClientSession`+`initialize()` with `Client`, splits types into\n  `mcp-types`, and diverts stdout while serving — all breaking for `mcp_server.py` +\n  `gen_mcp_reference.py`. Migration is epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b`; the pyproject\n  ceiling stays `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` (core L22 floor via `[mcp]` extra L82 + agents L215).\n  NEW urgency fact (recorded on 732b as part of this work): v2.0.0 is now the STABLE\n  release and v1.x is in maintenance mode (security fixes only), so `<2` is\n  time-bounded — but that changes the epic's priority, not this ticket's scope.\n* `json-repair` `0.62.0` -> `0.63.0` (minor) — SAFE. Usage surface:\n  `src/rebar/llm/structured.py` calls `repair_json(cand, return_objects=True[, schema=…])`\n  (L387-408); 0.63.0 adds None->null repair + fixes a `TrueBlue` mis-repair — both\n  strictly improve the tolerant-parse ladder; the called API is unchanged. pyproject\n  floor `json-repair>=0.61` (L132) already admits it: LOCK-ONLY.\n* `genai-prices` `0.1.1` -> `0.1.2` (patch) — SAFE. Pricing-data-only additions (new\n  model prices); consumed via optional lazy import in `usage_report.py`/`usage_log.py`\n  (`Usage` + `calc_price`, unchanged). pyproject has no pin (L150): LOCK-ONLY.\n* `botocore` `1.43.68` -> `1.43.69` (patch) — SAFE. Routine service-model update;\n  lazy imports only (`bedrock_model.py`, `structured.py`, `remote_cert.py`). Floor\n  `botocore>=1.43.0` (L291) admits it; boto3 1.43.68's botocore range (`<1.44`)\n  accepts 1.43.69, so boto3 itself need not move: LOCK-ONLY.\n\nThis ticket lands the three safe bumps only. No new mcp migration ticket is filed —\nepic 732b already owns it (per the #125/#127 precedent, tickets\ncarnivoral-consistent-lhasaapso and reclinable-ammonitic-hound / change 1812).\n\n## Approach\n\nIn a fresh worktree branched from `origin/main` (`../deps-128`, venv on PATH):\n\n1. NO pyproject.toml edit — verify with `git diff` that all three bumps are admitted\n   by existing constraints (floors listed above; exact pins exist for none of them).\n2. `uv lock --upgrade-package json-repair --upgrade-package genai-prices\n   --upgrade-package botocore` — the lock is regenerated by uv, never hand-edited\n   (CI gates on `uv lock --check`); then `uv sync --locked --extra dev --extra agents`\n   so gates run against the bumped versions.\n3. Verify the lock moved exactly the three intended packages to the PR's versions\n   (0.63.0 / 0.1.2 / 1.43.69) and `mcp` stayed 1.29.0; `git diff uv.lock` must show\n   no other version churn beyond uv's transitive bookkeeping for these three.\n4. Gates: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, `uv lock --check`, and targeted tests for\n   each usage surface: `pytest tests/unit/test_structured.py\n   tests/unit/test_silent_success.py tests/unit/test_usage_log.py\n   tests/unit/test_usage_log_pricing_qualified_2ca9.py` (json-repair + genai-prices\n   consumers) plus `tests/unit/test_llm_capabilities.py` if present (botocore lazy\n   import). Full `pytest tests/unit` is CI's job (host has pre-existing env git\n   failures documented on dc89-cd11-acd6-4e61); CI Verified +1 is the authoritative\n   full-suite gate.\n5. Commit (subject <=50 chars, body wrapped at 72) with trailer\n   `rebar-ticket: <this ticket's full canonical id>` + DCO `-s`;\n   `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`. Leave the ticket in_progress for the bots;\n   the change is submitted only after LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1.\n6. Comment on PR #128 (mcp rejected again per 732b, citing #124/#125/#127; safe\n   subset landing via the new Gerrit change); comment the v2-stable/v1-maintenance\n   urgency fact on epic 732b. Do NOT close the PR.\n\n7. SCOPE ADDITION (operator-approved 2026-08-15): stop the recurring mcp 2.0\n   re-proposals at the intake source. In .github/dependabot.yml's uv block, add\n   an ignore rule: dependency-name \"mcp\", update-types\n   [\"version-update:semver-major\"] — scoped to semver-major ONLY so 1.x\n   patch/security bumps still flow and security alerts stay on. Append a\n   one-line rationale to the header comment block: mcp major pinned out per\n   epic 732b-51df-acf2-477b (fastmcp import removal); remove the ignore when\n   the migration epic lands. Same commit as the safe-subset bump (same\n   intake-noise lane).\n\n## STOP / defer rule (explicit fallback done-state)\n\nIf ANY of the three bumps fails its targeted tests or lint/typecheck in step 4:\ndrop ONLY that package from the bump (re-run `uv lock --upgrade-package …` with the\nremaining packages from a clean `git checkout uv.lock`), record the failure evidence\nas a ticket comment, and land the remaining safe packages. The fallback done-state is\nAC2b: the ticket closes legitimately with a PARTIAL subset landed, provided every\ndropped package has a recorded-on-ticket failure reason. If ALL three fail, no lock change is pushed, but the dependabot.yml ignore\nrule (step 7 / AC7) still lands — as a standalone change carrying only\n.github/dependabot.yml — so the done-state is that standalone change merged\nplus the recorded failure evidence; the ticket then closes on AC2b's\nevidence path with zero lock bumps landed and AC7 satisfied.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n* mcp 2.0 migration (epic 732b) — the ceiling `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` is untouched.\n* boto3 version bump — not in PR #128 and not required by botocore 1.43.69.\n* Any src/rebar code change — nothing in the three deltas requires one.\n* `.github/complexity-baseline.json` — never touched by a deps change.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `uv.lock` on merged main records json-repair 0.63.0, genai-prices 0.1.2,\n  botocore 1.43.69 (or a documented AC2b subset), with mcp still 1.29.0 and\n  pyproject.toml unchanged; `uv lock --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] AC2: targeted usage-surface tests pass against the bumped versions\n  (test_structured.py, test_silent_success.py, test_usage_log.py,\n  test_usage_log_pricing_qualified_2ca9.py), and `make lint` + `make typecheck`\n  exit 0.\n- [ ] AC2b (fallback path): every package dropped under the STOP rule has a ticket\n  comment recording the concrete failure evidence and the re-lock excluding it; the\n  landed subset satisfies AC1 for the packages it retains. (Vacuously satisfied when\n  all three land.)\n- [ ] AC3: the change lands through Gerrit with a `rebar-ticket:` trailer for this\n  ticket's full canonical id + DCO sign-off, after LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1.\n- [ ] AC4: PR #128 carries a comment citing epic 732b + prior PRs #124/#125/#127 for\n  the mcp rejection and pointing at the Gerrit change; the PR is left open.\n- [ ] AC5: epic 732b-51df-acf2-477b carries a comment recording that mcp v2.0.0 is\n  the stable release and v1.x is maintenance-mode (security fixes only), i.e. the\n  `<2` ceiling is now time-bounded.\n- [ ] AC6: this ticket records a relates_to link to dc89-cd11-acd6-4e61\n  (reclinable-ammonitic-hound, the #127 precedent).\n- [ ] AC7: .github/dependabot.yml's uv block carries the mcp semver-major\n  ignore rule (patch/minor still flow; security alerts unaffected) and the\n  header comment records the 732b rationale + the removal trigger.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"uv.lock","reason":"regenerated by uv lock --upgrade-package for json-repair/genai-prices/botocore (lock-only; pyproject floors already admit them)"},{"path":".github/dependabot.yml","reason":"operator-approved scope addition: mcp semver-major ignore rule in the uv block + header rationale citing epic 732b, to stop recurring mcp 2.0 re-proposal PRs"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","3575-ea88-7b51-43c8"],["relates_to","dc89-cd11-acd6-4e61"],["relates_to","f700-8510-7823-4f27"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"24d611f4-9f94-4a0d-a9cc-5c9ff04f9b07","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c44a-2d4c-f793-42e6","ticket_type":"task","title":"deps: PR #128 safe subset (json-repair 0.63.0, genai-prices 0.1.2, botocore 1.43.69); mcp 2.0 deferred to 732b","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e8e3c52c-0273-49cc-be68-38414b490f67","454d5ebd-e3c7-46d9-bcea-4fd4fb4e4af8","98d4a6b5-38e3-4e6a-b057-f15bdcd0e541","0a483afa-54db-48ed-b491-8c4c3b098dce","24d611f4-9f94-4a0d-a9cc-5c9ff04f9b07","95fe6b0a-dd82-4585